{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1504082-rite-of-spirit-awakening-detail","id":1504082,"title":"Rite Of Spirit Awakening detail","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-28T15:51:05-08:00","id":1504082,"title":"Rite Of Spirit Awakening detail","content":"The W20 talk about bus, and the sanctification version about plants. As that gift work on most things what would give a sword/gun/tool awakened? The rank 1 homid gift description tell that it allows the garou to awake the spirit of any tool and the result is a difficulty reduction for 1 use, in v20 the first power of the Spiritus Discipline give some bonus dice for 1 use of an object spiritually awakened.<br /> <br /> Are those some possible effect of the rites and does the rite give a longer time for the effect? Or is it only a small boost that reinforce the object the same way it does on plants? What as a ST do you allows that rite to do or not do, cause the effect of the rite is different from the gift's but both talk about awakening the spirit of the object. <br /> <br /> Additionnal questions:<br /> -Does it work on fire, wind etc...?<br /> -Can you communicate with the awakened spirit (with some roll to understand some particularly alien spirits like roads, computer...)?<br /> -The rite tell you can't use it on conscient beings like humans, what would happen on non conscient beings (wolf, ants, fish)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T18:13:36-08:00","id":1504095,"title":"","content":"I would not conflate the mechanics for the Gift Apecraft's Blessing and the Rite of Spirit Awakening. Those are two separate things.<br /> <br /> That gift's description does say it &quot;awakens&quot; the tools spirit and causing it to lend its aid, but that is not the same as the Rite of Spirit Awakening. The gift is very focused - only tools, causing the spirit to lend its aid, and providing a specific purpose (lowered difficulty for one use). Furthermore even though the gift says it awakes the spirit, the spirit clearly does not stay awake afterward or can do anything else (talk, use charms, etc.) I would interpret the term &quot;awaken&quot; in this case very loosely. It's a one time favor, and that is all. It isn't truly awakened as an active spirit. In order to prevent confusion like this, it probably would have been better to use some other term than awaken, like &quot;engage&quot;.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Rite of Spirit Awakening does one thing - it wakens an inactive spirit from slumber. The spirit is active from that point on. It appears in the umbra, and can now do whatever the spirit wants. It is not even necessarily friendly to the person who awakened it as it can be hostile. You've just created an NPC and the ST now needs to roleplay it. There is no benefit in the material world. There is now just an active spirit of that object.<br /> <br /> If the spirit for some reason wants to be friendly and help out somebody using the object it inhabits, then I would say that something like a reduced difficulty or one bonus die is perfectly fine. But that is up to the spirit, and there's no reason why it would normally do so. Usually spirits require some form of chiminage to earn their favor. Otherwise the spirit just does what its nature wants it to do. It most likely does nothing. Or it might even cause trouble for whoever is using the object and adding to the difficulty or decreasing the die pool. It all depends on the spirit and its circumstances at that time. A gun whose spirit is awakened might decide its purpose is to kill and the gun becomes extremely dangerous to handle as it goes off by accident in order to kill people. A knife whose spirit is awakened might not like the way it is treated/handled by its owner, and just decide it isn't going to cut anymore. A car decides its like the owner who takes care of it so much that it dislikes the competition for attention from his new girlfriend, and runs her over like in the book and movie &quot;Christine&quot;. All sorts of odd things could be possible - it all depends on the ST running this new NPC.<br /> <br /> Can the rite be used on fire, wind, or other insubstantial things? The rite only mentions &quot;mundane objects&quot; and &quot;plants.&quot; That could imply it must require actual matter, but I don't think that was the intent. I think those were only mentioned in order to help guide the ST in those scenarios, and is not meant as a limit. Practically everything has a spirit, and as long as that spirit is slumbering it can be awakened. So I would interpret it loosely and say &quot;yes&quot;, it could waken a fire spirit or a wind spirit provided those things are &quot;present&quot; in the material world when the rite is performed. A fire kept in a grill or campfire is likely to be present for the rite, but a wind may not be - it might be there and gone before the rite could be completed. And depending on how the ST runs things, it might be that a very strong wind blowing in ALREADY has an active spirit guiding it in the Penumbra, and the rite wouldn't &quot;work&quot; because its spirit is not inactive. Those spirits would also not be bound to a specific object. An awakened wind spirit probably immediately moves on just as the wind does. A fire spirit would want the fire to keep spreading as the fire will die without &quot;food&quot; (which might put it back into slumber), and might start causing more fires because it can and want to - because that is what fire does. A lot more things could wrong if you awaken those kinds of spirits.<br /> <br /> We know the rite cannot work on &quot;sentient beings&quot; like humans, but what about other life forms? I know people who only use &quot;sentience&quot; in reference to humans (or other intelligent beings), and I know other people who apply sentience to various animals and distinguish humans from animals by using the term sapience. So what should an ST do? What was meant by the term? Well, we know that animal spirits are NOT the spirits of an individual animal. It's more like a platonic ideal of that species in general. So what is it that you are awakening in that individual animal? I think different STs will come to different conclusions, but for now I would not let the Rite of Spirit Awakening work on an animal any more than I would have it on a human. They are, in a sense, already &quot;awake&quot; in a way that objects and most plants (outside long lived trees) are not. Though I am open to changing my mind.<br /> <br /> Can you communicate with the awakened spirit? Yes, but in the same way you can talk with any spirit. The Rite does not provide any tools to do so. You likely need Spirit Speech to be able to communicate, but certain spirits might be able to communicate in certain ways to make some basic things known. If you awaken the spirit of a car, the spirit could likely honk its horn or flick its headlights on and off in the Penumbra. Remember, it's now an NPC spirit that behaves in whatever way the ST thinks such a spirit would act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T02:50:40-08:00","id":1504111,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> Now that's clearer. But now i know that this Rite awake a Spirit permanently (or at least until it is left without any interaction and slumber again) i wonder some other things: a spirit can grow in power with it's importance, i remember reading somewhere (the umbra book i think) that a simple gafflin spirit can become a jagglins when he become strong enough to represent it's forest in general. Let's take the exemple of an awaken sword handled by a garou for a long time and give him a small help (1bonus die, difficulty reduce by 1 or +1 damage die). With time and growing bond between the garou and the sword spirit, it would allow that spirit to become more powerfull and give better advantage to the Garou (or worst curse to one the spirit dislike). <br /> <br /> So eventually after (dozens) years of caring, respect, dedication to his friend/companion, the spirit could become powerfull enough to give it's garou difficulty reduced by 3, +5 die bonus, or double basic damage die (the +4 damage die of a double handed sword becoming 8 damage die).<br /> <br /> If you think it could work that way, would that mean a powerfull enough spirit awakened could turn it's object into a &quot;natural&quot; fetiche?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T12:30:26-08:00","id":1504132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1504082-rite-of-spirit-awakening-detail?p=1504111#post1504111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think it could work that way, would that mean a powerfull enough spirit awakened could turn it's object into a &quot;natural&quot; fetiche?</div> </div> </div> </div>In strict game terms, that would be a 'no' from me. Crafting a fetish (or talen) is a specific Rite to bind a spirit to an object, while waking a spirit does not do that. One could argue that the relationship between a spirit and an object it was awakened from is special in that it is the 'birthplace' of the spirit, but there is no indication that 'free' awakened spirits have a vital link or anything to it. What you would get would be an object that emulates the effects of a fetish through the actions of the spirit, but as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> mentioned, with even less reliability.<br /> <br /> Effectively, this would be the Numen Background - a Spirit ally that shares a social bond with the Garou. I'm not sure if that Background made it into W20, but earlier editions have it. There's a pact between the spirit and the Garou who offer each other mutual support (PG to Garou, p.170).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T17:09:52-08:00","id":1504149,"title":"","content":"While a spirit can grow in power over time or even transition from Gaffling to Jaggling, or even Jaggling to Incarna, I don't think that occurs in the limited time span of a chronicle. That would be a very long and drawn out process beyond the scope of the game's mechanics. At most, I might run a plot point in a chronicle where one specific spirit has grown in power because of some outside event or special reason. Likely it would be some Bane that has grown in power because of some terrible event that affects many people or a large territory. I wouldn't have some local spirit noticeably grow in power just because a PC shows it some friendship. A spirit might increase its Essence a bit during a chronicle, but we aren't going to see its other stats and powers increase.<br /> <br /> Nor would I allow an object with an active spirit essentially be a kind of magic device or fetish. We already have rules to do that - the Rite of Binding and the Rite of Fetish. If you want a fetish, then make a fetish. While we know the Rite of Spirit Awakening when done on plants sanctifies them and effectively turns them into a talen, that seems to be the exception. At most, as an ST I might provide an additional, brief bonus or penalty on a very rare basis. But it would be something I, as the ST, controls. I would not allow the player to demand when they get something, and certainly not provide them some kind of ongoing benefit.<br /> <br /> One thing that often gets overlooked by many players is they think the spirit should think the Garou (or more specifically their Garou) is special and showered with treats. But from the perspective of the spirit, the Garou are not their focus, and an individual Garou is not special. They have their own purposes, desires, and personalities. A sword spirit might not even want the PC that awakens it to handle it. Maybe it would rather be in the hands of someone who will routinely use it to kill, or prefers to be wielded by someone with higher Rage. Maybe it decides in the middle of your fight with a BSD Ahroun that it would rather be used by him and somehow betrays you - after all it is not a Gaian spirit. A rock spirit may quickly go back to slumber since it accomplished its mission by forming the planet billions of years ago, and it is now separated from others of its kind in the ore vein or quarry it was originally part of. So even if a Garou treats it &quot;well&quot;, it does not mean the spirit cares about that.<br /> <br /> So what is the benefit of wakening a spirit? There are several that I can see.<br /> <br /> One is that it causes objects to now appear in the Penumbra. Very few objects do. So an awakened car spirit must still be driven in the Real World, but a Garou in the Penumbra could still ride in it (but not drive it since the spirit continues to occupy the physical object). If you give someone an object with an awakened spirit in the real world, a Garou in the Penumbra can probably follow that person by following the spirit he sees in the Penumbra. The spirit probably observes its Penumbral surroundings in some capacity, and that might be of benefit.<br /> <br /> Another is that you now have a spirit you can interact with. Because it is the spirit of that sword, maybe that spirit might readily agree to the Rite of the Fetish since it is already its home - although we must keep in mind the most useful powers of a fetish is when you bind other kinds of spirits into an object. Still, maybe that sword spirit still provides some mechanical benefit to a fetish sword. The spirit might also be able to tell you information. The spirit of a crafted object might be able to tell you knowledge about how it was formerly used. The spirit of a natural object might retain some ancient memories or useful lore. And the spirit is now capable of teaching Gifts or using its Charms.<br /> <br /> This is how I would approach it as ST. Others might do differently. The main thing I would do is remember to treat it like an NPC. A spirit is a person, not a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T02:41:52-08:00","id":1504192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1504082-rite-of-spirit-awakening-detail?p=1504149#post1504149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a spirit can grow in power over time or even transition from Gaffling to Jaggling, or even Jaggling to Incarna, I don't think that occurs in the limited time span of a chronicle. That would be a very long and drawn out process beyond the scope of the game's mechanics. At most, I might run a plot point in a chronicle where one specific spirit has grown in power because of some outside event or special reason. Likely it would be some Bane that has grown in power because of some terrible event that affects many people or a large territory. I wouldn't have some local spirit noticeably grow in power just because a PC shows it some friendship. A spirit might increase its Essence a bit during a chronicle, but we aren't going to see its other stats and powers increase.<br /> <br /> Nor would I allow an object with an active spirit essentially be a kind of magic device or fetish. We already have rules to do that - the Rite of Binding and the Rite of Fetish. If you want a fetish, then make a fetish. While we know the Rite of Spirit Awakening when done on plants sanctifies them and effectively turns them into a talen, that seems to be the exception. At most, as an ST I might provide an additional, brief bonus or penalty on a very rare basis. But it would be something I, as the ST, controls. I would not allow the player to demand when they get something, and certainly not provide them some kind of ongoing benefit.<br /> <br /> One thing that often gets overlooked by many players is they think the spirit should think the Garou (or more specifically their Garou) is special and showered with treats. But from the perspective of the spirit, the Garou are not their focus, and an individual Garou is not special. They have their own purposes, desires, and personalities. A sword spirit might not even want the PC that awakens it to handle it. Maybe it would rather be in the hands of someone who will routinely use it to kill, or prefers to be wielded by someone with higher Rage. Maybe it decides in the middle of your fight with a BSD Ahroun that it would rather be used by him and somehow betrays you - after all it is not a Gaian spirit. A rock spirit may quickly go back to slumber since it accomplished its mission by forming the planet billions of years ago, and it is now separated from others of its kind in the ore vein or quarry it was originally part of. So even if a Garou treats it &quot;well&quot;, it does not mean the spirit cares about that.<br /> <br /> So what is the benefit of wakening a spirit? There are several that I can see.<br /> <br /> One is that it causes objects to now appear in the Penumbra. Very few objects do. So an awakened car spirit must still be driven in the Real World, but a Garou in the Penumbra could still ride in it (but not drive it since the spirit continues to occupy the physical object). If you give someone an object with an awakened spirit in the real world, a Garou in the Penumbra can probably follow that person by following the spirit he sees in the Penumbra. The spirit probably observes its Penumbral surroundings in some capacity, and that might be of benefit.<br /> <br /> Another is that you now have a spirit you can interact with. Because it is the spirit of that sword, maybe that spirit might readily agree to the Rite of the Fetish since it is already its home - although we must keep in mind the most useful powers of a fetish is when you bind other kinds of spirits into an object. Still, maybe that sword spirit still provides some mechanical benefit to a fetish sword. The spirit might also be able to tell you information. The spirit of a crafted object might be able to tell you knowledge about how it was formerly used. The spirit of a natural object might retain some ancient memories or useful lore. And the spirit is now capable of teaching Gifts or using its Charms.<br /> <br /> This is how I would approach it as ST. Others might do differently. The main thing I would do is remember to treat it like an NPC. A spirit is a person, not a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect, now i can work with my story, thanks a lot <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T22:54:02-08:00","id":1504245,"title":"","content":"I am glad my comments could be of help to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T19:35:45-08:00","id":1504323,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda disappointed that I didn't manage to participate in this thread more, but after Black Fox's responses I don't feel there is much to add. However, I will point out that awakening a spirit can be a big responsibility with consequences, and just like you probably wouldn't want a random child in the world, you might want to be careful what you awaken and how you treat it, as it may turn out quite poorly for everyone involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T16:06:38-08:00","id":1504787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1504082-rite-of-spirit-awakening-detail?p=1504323#post1504323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda disappointed that I didn't manage to participate in this thread more, but after Black Fox's responses I don't feel there is much to add. However, I will point out that awakening a spirit can be a big responsibility with consequences, and just like you probably wouldn't want a random child in the world, you might want to be careful what you awaken and how you treat it, as it may turn out quite poorly for everyone involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact one of my player asked if awake a spirit with the rite make it come to life or if ot was already &quot;alive&quot; but sleeping. Then i thought about it and since then i find the question interesting<br /> Are spirit born the same time as their physical part become important enough or for long enough? When can we tell a spirit is alive but sleeping? As everything in the umbra can be called spirits from rocks and wind to idea are they all sleeping gafflin? The core and Umbra books tells that in the Umbra things are composed with spiritual energy called ephemera, is that energy only energy or is it the &quot;basic&quot; material capable of turning into conscient being?<br /> So many question in only a week 0_0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T16:17:02-08:00","id":1504790,"title":"","content":"From what I understand everything is supposed to have a spirit, and a long time ago the Penumbra was absolutely filled with active spirits unlike the rather devoid place it is today. It's just that today almost all spirits are in slumber, and that living beings may have a spirit or soul that is already awake, but fails to be seen in the Penumbra unless they are in the Periphery or somehow &quot;spiritually strong&quot; that they can be seen in the Penumbra.<br /> <br /> Ephemera is simply the &quot;matter&quot; of the Middle Umbra. It isn't &quot;energy&quot; at all. I think the closest thing to energy would be Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T06:25:58-08:00","id":1504841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1504082-rite-of-spirit-awakening-detail?p=1504790#post1504790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I understand everything is supposed to have a spirit, and a long time ago the Penumbra was absolutely filled with active spirits unlike the rather devoid place it is today. It's just that today almost all spirits are in slumber, and that living beings may have a spirit or soul that is already awake, but fails to be seen in the Penumbra unless they are in the Periphery or somehow &quot;spiritually strong&quot; that they can be seen in the Penumbra.<br /> <br /> Ephemera is simply the &quot;matter&quot; of the Middle Umbra. It isn't &quot;energy&quot; at all. I think the closest thing to energy would be Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if i understand basically if something exist it has a spirit, the rite allows them to awake and communicate and when they slumber they can be seen or not in the penumbra depending on their importance or existance time.<br /> If ephemera is the &quot;matter&quot; that compose things in the umbra it compose also spirits themselves, logically","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}